{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468411-flux-weirdness-and-lost-worlds","id":1468411,"title":"Flux weirdness and lost worlds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-20T10:43:43-08:00","id":1468411,"title":"Flux weirdness and lost worlds","content":"I liked the idea of Flux and the idea that alternate worlds bleeding into each other is a big part of Trinity Continuum. It's a good explanation for how Daredevils, or Talents in this edition, are different then Quantum and Psi powered individuals but still are powered in some fashion. Lost Worlds potentially being other worlds bleeding into our world is also a good explanation for why adventurers could visit a lost city in Africa that is populated by sapient gorillas and nobody else can find it later. It's a meta reason for why the world pretty much keeps on track for the most part while adventurers can still go to these amazing places.<br /> <br /> But I was wondering if Lost World's or other Flux oddities are always going to be examples of cross time weirdness? One of the things I liked about the first version of Adventure! was that Z-Ray's propagated both backwards and forwards in time, so the Hammersmith Event could have been interpreted as having retroactively cause, for example, the Chiquibul caves having two civilizations of people living in it like something out of a Jules Verne story. Is Flux weirdness something that can be a permanent part of the world? Is things like that going to be more a part of the new version of Adventure!, with the &quot;modern day&quot; setting of the Trinity Continuum having Flux weirdness being more transitory crossovers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T11:02:05-08:00","id":1468413,"title":"","content":"Trinity Continuum has a lot of weirdness happening in plain sight, perfectly human doctors (with 8 tentacles, like any human), places where you can invoke ghosts of soldiers of past empires, machines that recorded people in a way you can interact with the record even years after the people are dead, machines that allow you to cross the mist to other realities (even possibly a invading army of reality invaders coming from another reality), among other things.<br /> <br /> Sure, Adventure has a lot of stuff, but it doesn\u2019t means they vanished the world, they are all there, people are just not going after it as they were in the 30s, and, if they are, they don\u2019t talk and out it as they used to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T14:23:48-08:00","id":1468427,"title":"","content":"Flux weirdness is already a permanent part of the world, the only thing that changes is the intensity, how many people find it and how many people talk about it, which varies from one era to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T15:56:43-08:00","id":1468433,"title":"","content":"Yeah makes me wonder about Flux weirdness in other eras. Like in Aeon. Does the odd perfectly human individual with 8 tentacles (as humans are known to have) get drowned out by the in your face psychic phenomena that is everywhere? It's probably also a little odd for people who are used to Flux weirdness when a new age starts up. When Nova's first started showing up how did people &quot;In the Know&quot; start realizing that this wasn't just a the oddity of the week and that it was the new normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T16:17:54-08:00","id":1468435,"title":"","content":"There is one book that have all kind of weirdness around Earth in Aeon Era, it\u2019s not all flux, but there are some, Terra Firma. There are some weirdness around the space too, Distant Worlds describe some of them, but also Under Alien Skies have some.<br /> <br /> Well, people \u201cin the know\u201d was aware about novas before N-Day and they know some of the weirdness were Quantum related. To be fair, the level of weirdness after Novas show up was so high they probably just didn\u2019t worry too much about flux anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T14:44:05-08:00","id":1468527,"title":"","content":"I actually came up with an odd character concept involving a Strange Place. An Inspired WWII soldier visited a Mythic China style Strange Place in the late 40s/early 50s, and got stuck there for decades due to fading Telluric energies. He eventually got back during the modern era, and is still in the prime of his life due to having eaten one of the peaches of immortality. This makes for a nice fish-out-of-water character, and lets you use an Adventure! era PC/NPC without having to bring in one of the big three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T15:03:02-08:00","id":1468529,"title":"","content":"Find and read the old Comic Book series Planetary. The Bleed would be exactly what you're looking for. The series can be bought on Amazon as a pair of graphic novels.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a strange world, let's keep it that way.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T09:25:21-08:00","id":1468599,"title":"","content":"I'm curious can novas and psiads interact with flux and visit list worlds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T10:34:39-08:00","id":1468603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468411-flux-weirdness-and-lost-worlds?p=1468599#post1468599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious can novas and psiads interact with flux and visit list worlds?</div> </div> </div> </div>If stalwarts and mesmerists can, then presumably novas and psions can as well. It is entirely possible that even baseline humans can wander into Strange Places. It is certainly genre appropriate for some reckless teens to find themselves in a spooky place and get killed or captured, necessitating the heroes to show up to investigate their disappearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T12:09:42-08:00","id":1468617,"title":"","content":"With the high Telluric energies of the Adventure! period it makes sense that there would be places were the worlds would touch firmly enough for ordinary people to cross. Even if these crossings we're limited in when and how someone could cross. <br /> <br /> In the Nova and/or Psion periods it takes having power (quantum, subquatum, whatever) in order to achieve a crossing. This is because lower Telluric energies allow greater stability which excludes complete openings between worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 11-23-2021, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T01:55:04-08:00","id":1468667,"title":"","content":"Well, I think the point is not crossing, it\u2019s opening the passage. Once it\u2019s open it\u2019s open and anyone can cross around, but open it is a job for a very powerful talent or random powerful flux events.<br /> <br /> There are passagens that are open for a few seconds, just enough to bring one person from another reality, and some stay open long enough to a lot of things happen, and there is the ones that power talents gifts, allowing just the gift to work.<br /> <br /> In Adventure they explain how it works for natural events, basically the more people know the world less probable the happening of a flux event is, in the 30s there was a loto o unknown parts and flux was free to fill the gaps, when people start exploring and mapping and everything the reality solidified a bit more until some weirdness disappear, the big ones first, but the small ones will be around longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T04:23:28-08:00","id":1468672,"title":"","content":"In our game we use the idea of guides. Say you visit a Dino swamp (Strange Place) in the 30s, then come back and live the rest of your life till the 2000s. You tell people about the dinosaur swamp you visited but they say it doesn't exist cause they've been to where you went and its not there. However if you decide to take them there your self the &quot;bridge&quot; for lack of a better word to the dino swamp is there when your guiding them so they can all visit it with you. It all comes down to belief. Even if someone tells you about a Strange Place (After Adventure! when it's much harder to get to them) there is always that small bit of doubt that it doesn't exist so the Flux probability don't collapse the right way and you can't find it, however by having someone lead you to it you avoid that outcome because they know the Strange Place is there and their certainty causes the Flux to reconnect the Strange Place to the world but only when they lead the expedition. It explains why in all these adventure movies and stories like The Mummy, Congo, Indiana Jones, or even the new Jungle Cruise move the main character always needs some sort of guide to get there.<br /> <br /> To be fair we also use the rule that observing something locks (for you at least) it in place on a Flux level. As in once you've seen a Strange Place yourself you can always go back there, but without seeing it yourself its a crap-shoot whether you can reach it. Evidence it exists helps you reach it if you've never seen it but it isn't certain and the more removed the evidence the less likely. Its why the note book with the route to the lost city is so important, sure a photocopy of the map might have the route on it but as it's a step removed from the main source it makes it harder i.e. adds complications to the roll to get to the Strange Place. Belief also plays a role, its why cults and the like are so prevalent in adventure stories. A strong enough belief in something collapses the probability state of the Flux to get the outcome you believe in. Basically a way for groups of people to unconsciously use dramatic editing. And also explains why the skeptic following the map can never find the Strange Place but the Hero can.<br /> <br /> This all grew out of explaining why Max Mercer can't change the past and won't talk about the future. Its because he watched the timeline collapsing that probability state for him. He saw it happen so he can't change it, and if he tells people what he saw because he is such a respected figure and they believe in him it prevents them from changing it as well. So he plays the mysterious benefactor and sends people on butterfly effect missions he doesn't explain to change the coming future. An indirect way of doing things but all he can do since he created so many fixed points in time he has to work around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T05:30:49-08:00","id":1468677,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27184_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27184\" data-vbnamecard=\"27184\">DarrenDalca</a> - I do not know what is official answer for the gameline, but your 'guides/belief' explanation is really nice one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm stealing it for my games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}